# MC-B-F3 (S:325). L §4.2 Differences: "month, quarter and year are one dimension of counted periods (§3.2), so two
# values of one period type, keys or not, differ by an int of periods ...: m - month_of(d) is the int number of months
# from month_of(d) to m, so month_of(d) + (m - month_of(d)) is m." d0 = 2025-01-15: 2025-01 - 2025-01 = 0 and
# 2025-04 - 2025-01 = 3 months; 2025-Q2 - 2025-Q1 = 1 quarter; the round trip gives m back. snap8 refused LOAD-UNIT
# "the difference of two month values that are not keys of one index".
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31

source s "s"
input d0: date question "a day?"

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  d0 = 2025-01-15 "a day"

def gap_m[m in months]: int = m - month_of(d0)
def gap_q[m in months]: int = quarter_of(start_of(m)) - quarter_of(d0)
def back[m in months]: month = month_of(d0) + (m - month_of(d0))

ask q: gap_m[m] for m in [2025-01, 2025-04] law 2025-12-31
ask qq: gap_q[2025-04] law 2025-12-31
ask r: back[2025-04] law 2025-12-31
=== expect
q (m = 2025-01): 0
  law date 2025-12-31, cut 2026-01-01
q (m = 2025-04): 3
  law date 2025-12-31, cut 2026-01-01
qq: 1
  law date 2025-12-31, cut 2026-01-01
r: 2025-04
  law date 2025-12-31, cut 2026-01-01
